# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Agent tooling — per-developer session state and caches, not project content.
# (oh-my-claudecode writes session logs, a HUD cache, and project memory here;
# these mutate on every run and are personal to whoever is working.)
.omc/

# Machine-local Plot state. The rest of `.plot` is project content (briefs,
# templates, the review hold) and stays committed; this holds caches describing
# THIS machine's refs and worktrees — the board's last-good pulse among them.
# A checked-in pulse would be one clone telling another what its branches are
# doing.
.plot/state/

# A dispatched worker's own traces, written into ITS worktree by
# `plot-dispatch.sh`: the pid it started, the exit code it ended with, and the
# console log in between. Machine-local for the same reason as `.plot/state/` —
# a checked-in pid describes a process on one laptop.
#
# Untracked and unignored is the worst of both: they show up in `git status`,
# and a `git add -A` in a worker's worktree carries someone's console log into
# the repo. Caught once, before it landed.
.plot-worker.pid
.plot-worker.wrapper.pid
.plot-worker.exit
.plot-worker.log
